{
  "_comment": [
    "Authored capability values, for what derivation cannot resolve.",
    "",
    "kitOf() turns a roster row into eleven 0-1 capability numbers using class, five",
    "boolean mechanics and a crowd-control depth. That is enough to place most",
    "champions, and not enough to tell three tank supports apart: Galio, Alistar and",
    "Rell come out with the IDENTICAL vector, because all three are a Tank that",
    "protects allies and carries three lockdown abilities. When vectors tie the",
    "ranking falls back to ladder strength, so whichever member of an archetype is",
    "strongest that patch wins every draft that calls for the archetype.",
    "",
    "These are hand-authored overrides, merged per FIELD, so a champion with one",
    "number here keeps the derived value for the other ten and a champion absent",
    "entirely is unaffected. It is deliberately partial: the supports the benchmark",
    "exercises, plus the marksmen the anti-tank draft needs. Extend it where the",
    "ranking is visibly wrong rather than trying to complete it.",
    "",
    "The numbers are judgements, not measurements. They should be argued with."
  ],
